// Pull request: #6091 Enrich ATT&CK tags (T1654/T1652) and dedupe bcdedit safeboot logic
// Pull request URL: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/pull/6091
// Pull request author: einlamye
// Change: update to existing rule
// Title: EventLog Query Requests By Builtin Utilities
// Sigma ID: 9cd55b6c-430a-4fa9-96f4-7cadf5229e9f
// Status: test | Level: medium
// Author: Ali Alwashali, Nasreddine Bencherchali (Nextron Systems)
// Date: 2023-11-20 | Modified: 2024-01-24
// ATT&CK: credential-access, discovery, T1552, T1654
// Tags: detection.threat-hunting
// Description: Detect attempts to query the contents of the event log using command line utilities. Attackers
//   use this technique in order to look for sensitive information in the logs such as passwords,
//   usernames, IPs, etc.
// False positives:
//   - Legitimate log access by administrators or troubleshooting tools
// References:
//   - https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/powershell/module/microsoft.powershell.diagnostics/get-winevent?view=powershell-7.3
//   - https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/powershell/module/microsoft.powershell.management/get-eventlog?view=powershell-5.1
//   - http://www.solomonson.com/posts/2010-07-09-reading-eventviewer-command-line/
//   - https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/windows-server/administration/windows-commands/wevtutil
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/6518cc50cd0ec1b32f3f086470293c355d6522f4/rules-threat-hunting/windows/process_creation/proc_creation_win_susp_event_log_query.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language, Defender schema)
// Machine-generated and not tested against real telemetry. Verify before use as a detection.

DeviceProcessEvents
| where (ProcessCommandLine contains "Select" and ProcessCommandLine contains "Win32_NTLogEvent") or ((FolderPath endswith "\\wevtutil.exe" or ProcessVersionInfoOriginalFileName =~ "wevtutil.exe") and (ProcessCommandLine contains " qe " or ProcessCommandLine contains " query-events ")) or ((FolderPath endswith "\\wmic.exe" or ProcessVersionInfoOriginalFileName =~ "wmic.exe") and ProcessCommandLine contains " ntevent") or (ProcessCommandLine contains "Get-WinEvent " or ProcessCommandLine contains "get-eventlog ")
